item.text:
Searches covered Egyptian presidential/state media, the Official Gazette and legal repositories, Arabic news and rights reporting, Sinai-specific documentation, prosecution/court records, and comparable execution data. They materially recover WD015’s wording and date, resolve WD008’s timing to July–August 2022, document a judicial remedy decision in the Hadhoud case, and establish a sharply mixed 2021–2022 death-penalty trajectory.

Important limits remain: I found no evidence of a presidential order authorizing the Sinai executions, no published investigation or discipline, and no publicly accessible official annex naming the 13 pardoned officers. Decree 13/2022 proves Sisi personally issued the applicable class-based pardon but does not identify its beneficiaries; the names and cases remain dependent on a leaked document reported by Arabi21. The recovered May 2 speech scapegoats the Brotherhood collectively, but the located words accuse its leaders of threatening violence rather than exhorting listeners to attack Brotherhood members. Minority-remedy searches yielded case-specific evidence, but source-family concentration remains substantial.

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON:{"title":"Sisi: Army had received three direct threats from the Brotherhood group","publisher":"Egypt State Information Service","publication_date":"2022-05-02","url":"https://sis.gov.eg/en/media-center/news/sisi-army-had-received-three-direct-threats-from-the-brotherhood-group/","claim":"In a May 2, 2022 intervention at an Eid celebration, Sisi said Muslim Brotherhood leaders had threatened to burn the country, conduct popular trials, kill, and bring fighters from elsewhere; he said he had avoided naming the Brotherhood for seven years and instead called it the 'people of evil' to give it an opportunity to retreat from evil. This is direct presidential scapegoating and threat-framing, but the located text contains no instruction to the public to attack Brotherhood members.","locator":"Article dated 2 May 2022; paragraphs beginning 'The president said that the army had received three direct threats' and 'For seven years I did not mention them'; official page is now indexed but intermittently returns 502","provisional_id":"WEB-3B-C1-001","canonical_fact_key":"sisi_2022_brotherhood_people_of_evil_speech","disposition":"final_evidence","chapter_ids":["3B"],"methodology_ids":["3B.3"],"source_type":"primary presidential speech record","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official state publication contemporaneous with the speech, although direct retrieval remains intermittently blocked.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact: 2 May 2022","ruler_attribution":"Direct words of Abdel Fattah el-Sisi.","contrary_evidence":"The same passage presents the label as restraint intended to allow retreat and does not expressly advocate violence against the group.","underlying_fact_key":"sisi_2022_brotherhood_people_of_evil_speech","lenses":["3B.3"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON:{"title":"Sisi reveals three times the Brotherhood threatened to burn Egypt","publisher":"El Watan","publication_date":"2022-05-02","url":"https://www.elwatannews.com/news/details/6069571","claim":"Contemporaneous Arabic reporting reproduces Sisi's extended wording: alleged threats to burn the country, conduct popular trials, kill, and bring fighters, followed by his statement that for seven years he used 'people of evil' instead of naming the Brotherhood. The complete passage supports classification as collective hostile labeling and alleged-threat narration, not an explicit call for listeners to commit violence.","locator":"Lines 83-93, especially quoted speech at lines 86-92","provisional_id":"WEB-3B-C1-002","canonical_fact_key":"sisi_2022_brotherhood_people_of_evil_speech_context","disposition":"final_evidence","chapter_ids":["3B"],"methodology_ids":["3B.3"],"source_type":"independent Arabic contemporaneous reporting","source_confidence":"medium-high","source_confidence_reason":"Named Egyptian news outlet reproducing a lengthy contemporaneous quotation and event setting; not institutionally independent enough to establish the underlying historical allegations.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact: 2 May 2022","ruler_attribution":"Direct quotation attributed to Sisi at a public event.","contrary_evidence":"The report supplies no evidence that the remarks produced violence and quotes Sisi describing his euphemism as an opportunity for the group to desist.","underlying_fact_key":"sisi_2022_brotherhood_people_of_evil_speech","lenses":["3B.3"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON:{"title":"Again: Videos show extrajudicial executions in Sinai by the military and its collaborators","publisher":"Sinai Foundation for Human Rights","publication_date":"2022-08-20","url":"https://sinaifhr.org/show/148","claim":"The Foundation located and analyzed videos appearing from early July through mid-August 2022 showing three separate close-range killings of unarmed, wounded, or restrained men, apparently by pro-military tribal fighters. The material appeared on accounts officially representing or operated by army-aligned groups. This materially resolves the events as most likely occurring during 2022 operations, while remaining an evidentiary assessment rather than a judicial finding.","locator":"Paragraphs 1-3 and video-specific sections; opened-page lines 52-60 and 81","provisional_id":"WEB-3B-C1-003","canonical_fact_key":"sinai_2022_three_custodial_executions","disposition":"final_evidence","chapter_ids":["3B"],"methodology_ids":["3B.2","3B.9"],"source_type":"local human-rights video investigation","source_confidence":"medium-high","source_confidence_reason":"Case-specific local investigation based on preserved visual material and account provenance; actor identification and exact filming dates remain probabilistic.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Strong: videos appeared July-August 2022 and were assessed as most likely depicting current 2022 hostilities.","ruler_attribution":"Authority-based national responsibility only; no evidence of Sisi ordering, knowing of, or approving the individual killings.","contrary_evidence":"The source repeatedly uses probabilistic language about perpetrators and dates and does not establish a presidential command chain for the executions.","underlying_fact_key":"sinai_2022_three_custodial_executions","lenses":["3B.2","3B.9"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON:{"title":"Sinai Tribes Union announces results of operation carried out alongside Egyptian army","publisher":"RT Arabic","publication_date":"2022-07-13","url":"https://arabic.rt.com/middle_east/1372154-%D9%85%D9%82%D8%AA%D9%84-%D8%A5%D8%B1%D9%87%D8%A7%D8%A8%D9%8A%D9%8A%D9%86-%D9%88%D8%A7%D9%84%D9%82%D8%A8%D8%B6-%D8%B9%D9%84%D9%89-%D8%A7%D8%AB%D9%86%D9%8A%D9%86-%D8%A2%D8%AE%D8%B1%D9%8A%D9%86-%D9%81%D9%8A-%D8%B3%D9%8A%D9%86%D8%A7%D8%A1/","claim":"A July 2022 statement attributed to the Sinai Tribes Union described its fighters conducting a sweep jointly with Egyptian Armed Forces combat formations and with full Egyptian Air Force cover. This corroborates operational integration between the militia and national forces during the same period as the execution videos, but does not establish authorization of the killings themselves.","locator":"Article heading and quoted Union statement: 'our heroes ... and combat formations of the Egyptian Armed Forces, with full cover from the Air Force, swept and cleared...'","provisional_id":"WEB-3B-C1-004","canonical_fact_key":"sinai_2022_militia_army_joint_operations","disposition":"context","chapter_ids":["3B"],"methodology_ids":["3B.2","3B.9"],"source_type":"Arabic reporting reproducing armed-group statement","source_confidence":"medium","source_confidence_reason":"Specific contemporaneous operational claim attributed to the participating militia, but published by a state-controlled foreign outlet and not an Egyptian command record.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Exact: operation reported 13 July 2022","ruler_attribution":"Supports accountable national-command context through joint operations; does not support a personal presidential order or knowledge.","contrary_evidence":"Joint operations and air cover do not prove that army commanders authorized or knew of separate executions.","underlying_fact_key":"sinai_2022_militia_army_joint_operations","lenses":["3B.2","3B.9"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON:{"title":"Republican Decree No. 13 of 2022 concerning pardons for Police Day and the January 25 Revolution","publisher":"Official Gazette of Egypt via Manshurat Legal","publication_date":"2022-01-23","url":"https://manshurat.org/node/75155","claim":"Sisi issued Decree No. 13/2022 granting remission of remaining custodial sentences to defined classes of prisoners effective January 25, generally including eligible prisoners who had completed one-third of their terms. The published decree proves direct presidential ownership of the pardon mechanism but does not name the 13 police personnel later reported as beneficiaries.","locator":"Decree heading and Article 1; second eligibility category reproduced at opened-page line 100","provisional_id":"WEB-3B-C1-005","canonical_fact_key":"egypt_decree_13_2022_police_day_pardon","disposition":"final_evidence","chapter_ids":["3B"],"methodology_ids":["3B.4","3B.9"],"source_type":"primary presidential decree","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official Gazette text reproduced by a specialist Egyptian legal repository.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact: January 2022 decree and eligibility date","ruler_attribution":"Direct: presidential decree issued by Sisi.","contrary_evidence":"The public text is class-based and contains no beneficiary names, so it cannot alone prove that particular convicted officers were pardoned.","underlying_fact_key":"egypt_2022_pardon_convicted_police_officers","lenses":["3B.4","3B.9"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON:{"title":"Presidential pardon for Egyptian officers implicated in torture cases (document)","publisher":"Arabi21","publication_date":"2022-04-27","url":"https://arabi21.com/story/1434502/%D8%B9%D9%81%D9%88-%D8%B1%D8%A6%D8%A7%D8%B3%D9%8A-%D8%B9%D9%86-%D8%B6%D8%A8%D8%A7%D8%B7-%D8%A8%D9%85%D8%B5%D8%B1-%D9%85%D8%AA%D9%88%D8%B1%D8%B7%D9%8A%D9%86-%D9%81%D9%8A-%D9%82%D8%B6%D8%A7%D9%8A%D8%A7-%D8%AA%D8%B9%D8%B0%D9%8A%D8%A8-%D9%88%D8%AB%D9%8A%D9%82%D8%A9","claim":"Arabi21 reported, based on a displayed official-looking document and an unnamed senior security source, that 13 officers and policemen convicted in three torture-to-death cases were released under Sisi's Police Day pardon. It identifies one matter as Case 8414/2018, Hadaiq al-Qubba felonies, concerning Ahmed al-Sayed Mohamed Agami. This upgrades the allegation with a case number but remains leaked-document reporting, not a published beneficiary annex.","locator":"Paragraphs 1-3 and case sections; opened-page lines 58-64 and 85; embedded document image linked after paragraph naming Case 8414/2018","provisional_id":"WEB-3B-C1-006","canonical_fact_key":"egypt_2022_pardon_convicted_police_officers_names","disposition":"final_evidence","chapter_ids":["3B"],"methodology_ids":["3B.4","3B.9"],"source_type":"investigative Arabic reporting based on leaked document","source_confidence":"medium","source_confidence_reason":"Provides a document image, case number, victims, and detailed convictions, and was later repeated by the U.S. State Department; the document is not independently published in the Gazette and the security source is anonymous.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact: reported April 2022 concerning the January 2022 pardon","ruler_attribution":"Direct if the beneficiary document is authentic, because it links named convicted officers to Sisi's Decree 13/2022.","contrary_evidence":"The official public decree contains no names, leaving the decisive beneficiary link dependent on a leak and anonymous sourcing.","underlying_fact_key":"egypt_2022_pardon_convicted_police_officers","lenses":["3B.4","3B.9"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON:{"title":"The Prosecution dismisses AFTE’s request to reopen investigation into Ayman Hadhoud’s death","publisher":"Association for Freedom of Thought and Expression","publication_date":"2022-06-23","url":"https://afteegypt.org/en/legal-profiles-en/legal-news-en/2022/04/24/30223-afteegypt.html","claim":"On June 23, 2022, New Cairo Criminal Court Circuit 28 upheld the Nasr City Prosecution's no-prosecution decision in Case 738/2022 concerning Ayman Hadhoud's custodial death and rejected the family's civil claim. The defense had sought access to the file, further witnesses, and expert review of the unpublished autopsy. This establishes that a formal review remedy was pursued and denied; the criticisms of the investigation are the defense's allegations, not court findings.","locator":"Chronology entries dated 23 June, 20 June, and 1 June 2022; opened-page lines 97-107","provisional_id":"WEB-3B-C1-007","canonical_fact_key":"hadhoud_2022_prosecution_closure_and_appeal","disposition":"final_evidence","chapter_ids":["3B"],"methodology_ids":["3B.4","3B.9"],"source_type":"case-specific legal monitoring record","source_confidence":"medium-high","source_confidence_reason":"Provides court, circuit, case number, dates, disposition, and pleaded requests; written by counsel-side civil society rather than the court itself.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact: June 2022 judicial decisions","ruler_attribution":"Institutional remedy evidence only; no source establishes Sisi's personal intervention in the investigation or appeal.","contrary_evidence":"The prosecution's forensic position was that death resulted from chronic heart disease without criminal violence, and a criminal court upheld closure; independent experts and the family disputed the investigation's adequacy.","underlying_fact_key":"hadhoud_2022_prosecution_closure_and_appeal","lenses":["3B.4","3B.9"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON:{"title":"Egyptian Public Prosecution denies criminal suspicion in the death of Hadhoud","publisher":"Egypt State Information Service / Egyptian Public Prosecution","publication_date":"2022-04-23","url":"https://sis.gov.eg/en/media-center/news/egyptian-public-prosecution-denies-criminal-suspicion-in-the-death-of-hadhoud/","claim":"The Public Prosecution stated that its investigation and Forensic Medicine Authority autopsy found Hadhoud died from chronic heart disease and that his body bore no injury indicating criminal violence. This is important contrary official evidence, but it does not resolve independent criticisms concerning withheld records, delayed family notification, alleged injuries, or investigative independence.","locator":"Article paragraphs summarizing the prosecution's completed investigation, autopsy conclusion, and absence of injury; direct page intermittently returns 502 but indexed text is available","provisional_id":"WEB-3B-C1-008","canonical_fact_key":"hadhoud_2022_official_no_crime_finding","disposition":"final_evidence","chapter_ids":["3B"],"methodology_ids":["3B.4"],"source_type":"primary prosecution finding republished by state authority","source_confidence":"medium-high","source_confidence_reason":"Official contemporaneous account of the prosecution and forensic conclusion; underlying autopsy and full investigation file were not published for independent inspection.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact: April 2022 investigation","ruler_attribution":"National institutional response only; no personal presidential role established.","contrary_evidence":"Independent forensic reviewers and family counsel alleged visible injuries and serious omissions; the official autopsy itself was not publicly released.","underlying_fact_key":"hadhoud_2022_prosecution_closure_and_appeal","lenses":["3B.4"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON:{"title":"Egypt: Release nine Coptic Christians detained for attempting to rebuild church","publisher":"Amnesty International Arabic","publication_date":"2022-03-30","url":"https://www.amnesty.org/ar/latest/news/2022/03/egypt-release-nine-coptic-christians-detained-for-attempting-to-rebuild-church/","claim":"Nine Coptic residents of Ezbet Farag Allah were detained after peacefully protesting the prolonged refusal to permit reconstruction of their burned church; National Security questioned them and Supreme State Security Prosecution ordered pretrial detention on assembly and terrorism-related allegations. The case supplies Arabic, case-specific evidence that protection/remedy mechanisms could instead expose minority claimants to coercion.","locator":"Case chronology and sections 'استجواب دون حضور محامين' and 'التمييز ضد المسيحيين'; opened-page lines 74-77","provisional_id":"WEB-3B-C1-009","canonical_fact_key":"ezbet_farag_allah_copts_church_rebuild_detention_2022","disposition":"final_evidence","chapter_ids":["3B"],"methodology_ids":["3B.7"],"source_type":"Arabic case-specific human-rights investigation","source_confidence":"medium-high","source_confidence_reason":"Names the village, dates, authorities, procedural steps, and legal allegations; advocacy source rather than primary prosecution file.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact: arrests and prosecution in January-February 2022","ruler_attribution":"National security and prosecution conduct under Sisi's government; no personal presidential order established.","contrary_evidence":"The state formally characterizes the church-building law as protective, and this source does not provide the prosecution's evidentiary case beyond the stated charges.","underlying_fact_key":"ezbet_farag_allah_copts_church_rebuild_detention_2022","lenses":["3B.7"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON:{"title":"Fire at Abu Sefein Church not due to foul play: Prosecution","publisher":"Ahram Online","publication_date":"2022-08-18","url":"https://english.ahram.org.eg/NewsContent/1/1233/473435/Egypt/Courts--Law/Fire-at-Abu-Sefein-Church-not-due-to-foul-play-Pro.aspx","claim":"Following the deadly Abu Sefein Coptic church fire, the Public Prosecution investigated and concluded that an electrical short, rather than criminal or sectarian foul play, caused the fire. This is case-specific contrary evidence against treating every 2022 Coptic mass-casualty event as identity-based violence.","locator":"Headline and first substantive paragraph, opened-page lines 47-57","provisional_id":"WEB-3B-C1-010","canonical_fact_key":"abu_sefein_church_fire_2022_prosecution_finding","disposition":"context","chapter_ids":["3B"],"methodology_ids":["3B.7"],"source_type":"local reporting of prosecution finding","source_confidence":"medium-high","source_confidence_reason":"Clear contemporaneous report of a specific official investigative conclusion; the complete prosecution file is not linked.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Exact: August 2022 event and finding","ruler_attribution":"National investigative response only; no personal presidential role.","contrary_evidence":"The finding addresses causation of this fire, not broader concerns about church safety regulation, emergency response, or minority protection.","underlying_fact_key":"abu_sefein_church_fire_2022_prosecution_finding","lenses":["3B.7"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON:{"title":"Death Sentences and Executions 2022","publisher":"Amnesty International","publication_date":"2023-05-16","url":"https://www.amnesty.org/en/wp-content/uploads/2023/05/ACT5065482023ENGLISH.pdf","claim":"Amnesty recorded 24 executions and at least 538 new death sentences in Egypt during 2022. Compared with its separately compiled 2021 figures, executions fell sharply from at least 83 while new death sentences rose from at least 356. The trajectory therefore does not support an unqualified claim that state coercion broadly declined alongside reduced insurgent activity.","locator":"PDF page 26, Middle East and North Africa country table, Egypt row; extracted lines 1024-1033","provisional_id":"WEB-3B-C1-011","canonical_fact_key":"egypt_death_penalty_2022_amnesty_counts","disposition":"final_evidence","chapter_ids":["3B"],"methodology_ids":["3B.10"],"source_type":"annual cross-national monitored dataset/report","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Stable annual methodology and explicit country-year table; figures are confirmed minima because Egyptian death-penalty information is not fully transparent.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact: calendar year 2022","ruler_attribution":"State judicial and executive coercion during Sisi's presidency; figures do not establish his personal decision in every case.","contrary_evidence":"Recorded executions decreased substantially, which is favorable on that measure, but death sentencing increased by roughly half.","underlying_fact_key":"egypt_death_penalty_2021_2022_trajectory","lenses":["3B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON:{"title":"Death Sentences and Executions 2021","publisher":"Amnesty International","publication_date":"2022-05-24","url":"https://www.amnesty.org/en/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/ACT5054182022ENGLISH.pdf","claim":"Amnesty recorded at least 83 executions and at least 356 death sentences in Egypt in 2021. Used as the fixed prior-year comparator, these figures show that the 2022 decline in executions coincided with a large rise in new death sentences rather than an across-the-board reduction in state lethal-coercion exposure.","locator":"PDF page 38, Middle East and North Africa table, Egypt row; extracted lines 1452-1461","provisional_id":"WEB-3B-C1-012","canonical_fact_key":"egypt_death_penalty_2021_amnesty_counts","disposition":"final_evidence","chapter_ids":["3B"],"methodology_ids":["3B.10"],"source_type":"annual cross-national monitored dataset/report","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Stable annual methodology and explicit country-year table; values are minimum confirmed counts.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Comparator: exact calendar year 2021","ruler_attribution":"State judicial and executive coercion during Sisi's presidency; not personal attribution for each sentence or execution.","contrary_evidence":"The much higher 2021 execution count makes the 2022 fall material and should not be obscured by the rise in death sentences.","underlying_fact_key":"egypt_death_penalty_2021_2022_trajectory","lenses":["3B.10"]}
